{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/226625-is-the-transition-to-grump-really-that-horrible","id":226625,"title":"Is the transition to Grump really that horrible?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-12T17:31:27-07:00","id":226625,"title":"Is the transition to Grump really that horrible?","content":"I keep reading how you die inside by growing up (and I hate that part of the game along with the significance given to the Childling/Wilder/Grump nonsense for so many reasons) but I just don't see it really reflected in the mechanics. What is so bad about being a Grump and getting old that cannot be rectified by a little XP spent on boosting your Glamour and some work at reducing your permanent Banality score?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T18:02:41-07:00","id":226644,"title":"","content":"For me Grump is where Changeling actually begins. Everything else is prelude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T18:09:50-07:00","id":226651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I keep reading how you die inside by growing up </div> </div> </div>Some of most creative and imaginative people in the world are not much young, so that's quite ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T18:20:56-07:00","id":226660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/226625-is-the-transition-to-grump-really-that-horrible?p=226651#post226651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some of most creative and imaginative people in the world are not much young, so that's quite ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. I only began to truly come to life on the inside when I got older, wiser and saw the world through the eyes of multiple perspectives and experience. And yet, by game statistics I should be more dead inside, and more numb to wonder because I am older and demand proof for outrageous claims. As if filtering out what is false and gazing out at the majesty of the cosmos is really boring and banal. <br /> <br /> When you get older you live see a broader world than when you were merely a child, that has its own Glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 08-12-2014, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T21:45:58-07:00","id":226780,"title":"","content":"I think the idea of Grumptom being mandatory with older age needs to be adjusted. Maybe I just knew some whacky old geezers that seem to me like they would be Wilders if you made them Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T06:56:20-07:00","id":226990,"title":"","content":"I find all three of the seemings pretty problematic as written. I'm hoping that they can be renamed/redefined if not dropped altogether if there's a Changeling 20th.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T12:51:32-07:00","id":227268,"title":"","content":"Changelings are horribly ageist, Grumphood reminds them that they are no longer immortal fairy dream creatures but things that will die. This is doubly so for the Sidhe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T09:21:53-07:00","id":228056,"title":"","content":"I think that a number of the above posters are missing the point on several keys aspects: while it is perfectly fine for you all to feel &quot;x&quot; about the aging aspect of Changeling, you have to remember that you *are not* playing a human character, but a *Changeling* -- their innate feelings and reactions to certain things are going to be very different in many regards from that of a human being's. (If fact, in that context, Changelings are much more removed from a conventional human perspective than most all vampires, werewolves (even the Red Talons), mages, wraiths, mummies, et al.; that point cannot be stressed enough...) Also, it's important to note that the whole &quot;tiered aging&quot; aspect is very much in-sync with many legends/mythic perspectives concerning the Fae and similar beings: many of the more wild, flighty ones *are* young -- either childlike in appearance, or an adolescent/teenager, by human standards -- while the more &quot;sedate&quot; (relatively speaking) beings are older in appearance/demeanor/mein (Oberon and Titania are excellent examples, as are the bridge trolls and garden gnomes of more common myths). That doesn't mean that the &quot;older&quot; changelings can't still be pranksters or fanciful, nor that the Childlings can't be millennia old and display a peculiar wisdom about the world (albeit in a manner that most mortals don't immediately fathom), just that the &quot;younger&quot; end of the scale is usually more capricious and whimsical, while the &quot;older&quot; end of the scale is more calm/focused, by comparison.<br /> <br /> It also bears out that much of the ageism in the game is *in-narrative*, a perception that many &quot;younger&quot; (Childling and Wilder) fae have about the &quot;old Grumps&quot; that occurs *in the story*, but isn't quite as true outside that perspective; while the game mechanics definitely show differences stat-wise, it is all balanced in the end: Childlings have certain advantages/comparative drawbacks, Wilders are in a &quot;middle ground&quot;, while Grumps are less (G)lamour(ous) but consequently more solid in their purposes and able to &quot;follow through&quot; on their intentions better than the &quot;younger&quot; lot (more Willpower). Just because the Childlings/Wilders *think* the Grumps are &quot;not with it&quot; (and there is *some* truth to that), that doesn't mean that that perception is, in fact, *true*. PLENTY of vampires, mages, werewolves, etc., have *in-narrative* perspectives about other splats (including their own) that are talked about in-narratively (with resulting social pressure applied to &quot;prove&quot; the &quot;truth&quot; behind such assertions), even though the game mechanics/meta-narrative prove otherwise. Same thing here: Grumps can be every bit as magical as the &quot;younger&quot; ones -- they just have to work harder at it. And vice-versa: the Childlings/Wilders can potentially have the same will/focus as the Grumps -- they, also, just have to work harder at it (though not many are so inclined).<br /> <br /> I've never had a problem with the three tiers in Changelings -- I thought it was great concept that conveyed an important metaphysical aspect of Changeling/Fae existence. Of course, some (obviously) may not like it, but then it's very easy to tweak this aspect with no real work at all (Childlings can span from toddler to 18-ish; Wilders from late teens to 20's/&quot;young looking&quot; 30's; Grumps from mature-looking 20's to any age after). Or it's easy enough to tweak it so that *apparent*/mein age isn't representative of the inner-essence of the Changeling: the 3 tiers can simply be &quot;essence-assessments&quot;, with the Childling/Wilder/Grump *appearance* merely being suited to the individual personality of the character in question: an older (30+) looking fae can be a Childling in essence, while that 5 year-old in the corner can be a Grump, despite her looking like she's in kindergarten. Easy-peasy. No big whoop. A simple tweak. Done.<br /> <br /> &gt;shrugs&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T10:12:53-07:00","id":228154,"title":"","content":"Q: Is being a grump horrible?&quot;<br /> A: Get the hell off my glen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/226625-is-the-transition-to-grump-really-that-horrible?p=228056#post228056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that a number of the above posters are missing the point on several keys aspects: while it is perfectly fine for you all to feel &quot;x&quot; about the aging aspect of Changeling, you have to remember that you *are not* playing a human character, but a *Changeling* -- their innate feelings and reactions to certain things are going to be very different in many regards from that of a human being's. (If fact, in that context, Changelings are much more removed from a conventional human perspective than most all vampires, werewolves (even the Red Talons),</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not possible. Red Talons, Lupus and Metis have never been human and never will be. Changelings are plunked into a human existence as, more or less a part of it, and live out a considerable amount of their life among ordinary humans, and have a perspective that allows ordinary humans to exist without wanting to claw the ever-loving shit out of those humans for what said humans have done, aided and abided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T10:53:20-07:00","id":228210,"title":"","content":"There are also valid out of character concerns about the three seemings. The unintentional glorification of underage sex is one. It's why childlings and wilders had to be banned on White Wolf's on-line game, New Bremen, back in the day.<br /> <br /> As said, it wouldn't take much to redefine them into something less problematic. Making them milestones for certain points of no return as a character accumulates more banality and becomes more world weary instead of being tied to physical age would be a good start. If that were to happen, they should probably get a new name to reflect their new function. The old names could be kept as slang terms if they need to still exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T13:06:07-07:00","id":228404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/226625-is-the-transition-to-grump-really-that-horrible?p=228154#post228154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Q: Is being a grump horrible?&quot;<br /> A: Get the hell off my glen.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's not possible. Red Talons, Lupus and Metis have never been human and never will be. Changelings are plunked into a human existence as, more or less a part of it, and live out a considerable amount of their life among ordinary humans, and have a perspective that allows ordinary humans to exist without wanting to claw the ever-loving shit out of those humans for what said humans have done, aided and abided.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realized I should have clarified what my point was with that -- upon re-reading, I can see how it would be misinterpreted. I don't mean simply in terms of human society, but rather in terms of metaphysical existence vis-a-vis their connection to the chimerical/The Dreaming. Even the most human-hating Red Talon has a connection closer to the human world (via Gaia and the Middle Umbra) than the Fae/Changelings do when &quot;awakened&quot; to their fae natures. Similar thing with Metis and Lupus Garou: while not born into a human form, they are still partly human (per Werewolf), and in all but the rarest cases still interact with the human world, by-and-large, in some capacity. When talking about the essence of the Changelings, and where they are along their &quot;maturation process&quot; (so to speak), they are quite removed on several metaphysical levels from normal human existence: this is more on point when you have (in the extreme example) a Childling who appears as an 8 year old but is well unto several millennia old, or a particularly despondent 19 year old (in human years) who has -- via Banality and some bad life experiences -- already &quot;matured&quot; to looking 50+ years old (again, by human reckoning). This isn't so much about how removed from human cultures the Changeling is, but rather how different his very essence/existence is from mundane reality. (Even with the case of, say, vampires and wraiths, the former is often quite connected to people despite being metaphysically quite different from them, but still a semblance of being human, and only becomes truly removed -- though not in all cases -- as the centuries become millennia; with wraiths, they are still very much &quot;themselves&quot; -- humans-made-ephemeral -- and by the time they become truly something a step-to-the-left metaphysically different, they most often no longer have any connections to the Skinlands/Shadowlands, and are removed to the deeper Low Umbra.) I've played Changeling, in different groups, since it came out two decades ago, and I remember some of the problems some players had with it back then, in terms of the very points the OP is bringing up. I posted then more-or-less what I posted here (and further above), and I stand by it as both the rationale behind 'x&quot;, as well as citing very simple examples of how it can be tweaked with no muss, no fuss. <br /> <br /> Just saying...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T13:12:33-07:00","id":228435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/226625-is-the-transition-to-grump-really-that-horrible?p=228210#post228210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are also valid out of character concerns about the three seemings. The unintentional glorification of underage sex is one. It's why childlings and wilders had to be banned on White Wolf's on-line game, New Bremen, back in the day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, well yes -- *that* was/is a completely different consideration altogether, in terms of the real-life thing. I agree now and did then with WWs not allowing certain imagery/forms of discussion relative to that to occur, for obvious reasons...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T09:22:53-07:00","id":229115,"title":"","content":"I hope that some of the changes discussed above separating the age castes from actual chronological age can be integrated into C20 (if it comes to pass). In addition to the crazy creative clockwork mad inventor-style knocker who is in his 70's but is still a Childling, I like the idea of a solemn Wednesday Addams-like sluagh Grump who appears to be a 5 yr old girl. In fact, I really like that she might ACTUALLY be 5 yrs old and just came into her own as a Grump. Or that she might be quite old and just appear to be 5 yrs old for some reason. (Though that might be a Merit/Flaw thing). <br /> <br /> It MIGHT be a minor enough fix to slide into a 20th Anniversary edition. Overall, it looks like the changes made in the games so far aren't really substantive (e.g. Mage will still be running with insanely small die pools to do anything magical, etc.) So, if it's seen as &quot;part of the game as it was&quot; forChildlings being teens, Wilders being tweens and Grumps being anything over the age of consent (exaggerating here, but not as much as it should be), we won't see much of a change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T09:45:49-07:00","id":229136,"title":"","content":"David Hill's quote over in the KotE thread makes me think some mechanical changes can get put in as long as the game still <i>feels</i> like Changeling: The Dreaming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/186083-i-think-kote-may-be-salvageable-for-a-20th-anniversary-run?p=220656#post220656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is not necessarily true. Some of the X20 stuff is more dramatically different than others. We've had some wonderful leeway in V20 Dark Ages, despite it being beholden to V20 in some ways. This is an assumption based on the mission statements for certain products, assuming they carry over to all products.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But really, I'm just guessing. I'm hoping we'll find out a little bit more tomorrow!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T19:19:11-07:00","id":229844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/226625-is-the-transition-to-grump-really-that-horrible?p=229136#post229136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">David Hill's quote over in the KotE thread makes me think some mechanical changes can get put in as long as the game still <i>feels</i> like Changeling: The Dreaming.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But really, I'm just guessing. I'm hoping we'll find out a little bit more tomorrow!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I remember way back one of the developers of Changeling talked about some of the changes he wished he could make. Primal, for instance, was going to get split up into two different Arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}